# Tauri desktop build (vite build --mode desktop). Loaded ONLY by
# `npm run build:desktop`, which is what `tauri build` invokes.
#
# Why this exists separately from .env.cloud:
# The cloud build ships behind a Vercel rewrite (relative /api-02
# path, resolved server-side). Tauri has no such proxy — the
# WebView loads pages from the custom protocol `http://tauri.localhost`,
# so a relative fetch would hit Tauri's asset server and get back
# the SPA index.html (200 OK, text/html). That's why the built shell
# used to fail login with "Login response was empty or malformed".
#
# The desktop shell needs an ABSOLUTE URL. The default here targets
# the local API for dev testing; for a customer install, either:
#   1. Rebuild with this file overridden to the customer's host, OR
#   2. Ship the default and have the installed app write
#      localStorage['hrms:apiBaseOverride'] at first run.
VITE_API_BASE=http://198.211.108.211:4000
